      "message": "Thanks for working on this! While testing edge cases, I found a couple of issues with the current approach and uploaded a companion CL on top of yours to demonstrate both the failing tests and a cleaner fix:\nhttps://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1396817\n- Patchset 1 adds 4 unit tests that fail on this CL (9 failing assertions).\n- Patchset 3 has the complete fix (all 19 `SkParagraph_SoftHyphen*` tests pass, and we can also drop `Run::fHyphen` / `Run::isHyphen()`).\n\nSpecifically:\n\n1. **Double-counting `U+00AD` in `getRectsForRange`:**\n   Because the line-final `U+00AD` cluster is still part of the normal text run (`!run-\u003eisEllipsis()`), not skipping `fHyphen` causes `getRectsForRange` to measure the soft hyphen twice: once in the normal text run (as a 0-width / invisible cluster) and once in `fHyphen`.\n   In simple LTR cases `ClipContext::merge()` happens to merge the 0-width box with `fHyphen`\u0027s box, but that breaks whenever the two boxes cannot be merged or when the invisible cluster is spaced:\n   - **Fallback font (`SkParagraph_SoftHyphenFallbackFontRect`):** when `fHyphen` uses a fallback font (`lastRun-\u003efont() !\u003d context.run-\u003efont()`), `merge()` does not combine them, so `getRectsForRange(softHyphen, softHyphen + 1)` returns 2 boxes (`boxes[0]` with width 0, `boxes[1]` with width \u003e 0) and `getGlyphInfoAtUTF16Offset(softHyphen)` (which reads `boxes[0]`) returns a 0-width rect.\n   - **Letter spacing (`SkParagraph_SoftHyphenLetterSpacingRect`):** `addLetterSpacesEvenly()` adds `letterSpacing` to the invisible `U+00AD` cluster in the text run, which merges with `fHyphen` and shifts `hyphenExtent.first` left by `letterSpacing`.\n   - **BiDi (`SkParagraph_SoftHyphenBidiRect`):** for an LTR word broken at a soft hyphen inside an RTL paragraph, `fHyphen` is placed at the left edge of the line while the unexcluded `U+00AD` cluster in the LTR text run emits a 0-width box at the right edge, making the soft-hyphen extent span the entire line width.\n\n2. **Sizing `fHyphen-\u003efTextRange` in `createSoftHyphen()` instead of checking `run-\u003eisHyphen()`:**\n   In `TextLine::createSoftHyphen()`, if we set:\n   ```cpp\n   fHyphen-\u003efTextRange \u003d TextRange(0, lastCluster.textRange().width());\n   ```\n   then `iterateThroughSingleRunByStyles` (which already constructs `TextRange testRange(run-\u003efClusterStart, run-\u003efClusterStart + run-\u003etextRange().width())` and always returns `run-\u003eadvance().fX` for `run-\u003eisEllipsis()`) automatically maps `fHyphen` to the `U+00AD` cluster\u0027s source range regardless of `hyphenStr`\u0027s UTF-8 byte length and always reports `run-\u003eadvance().fX` for `*runWidthInLine`.\n   Combined with clamping normal text runs on hyphenated lines in `getRectsForRange`:\n   ```cpp\n   if (fHyphen !\u003d nullptr \u0026\u0026 !run-\u003eisEllipsis()) {\n       textRange \u003d textRange * TextRange(fTextIncludingNewlines.start, fHyphen-\u003efClusterStart);\n   }\n   ```\n   we don\u0027t need the `if (run-\u003eisHyphen())` block in `getRectsForRange` or `Run::fHyphen` / `Run::isHyphen()` at all.\n\n3. **Same RTL `runOffsetInLine` bug in `getGlyphPositionAtCoordinate` (`SkParagraph_SoftHyphenGlyphPositionAtCoordinateRtl`):**\n   `getGlyphPositionAtCoordinate` had the same RTL offset bug that you noticed in `getRectsForRange`: in RTL, `fHyphen` / `fEllipsis` is visited first at the left edge, and `if (run-\u003eisEllipsis())` returned `false` without setting `*runWidthInLine \u003d run-\u003eadvance().fX` (while `iterateThroughVisualRuns` ignored the `false` return in RTL). That shifted hit-testing for all subsequent RTL runs on the line left by `hyphenWidth`. Setting `*runWidthInLine \u003d run-\u003eadvance().fX` and only stopping on `run-\u003eisEllipsis()` in LTR or when `dx \u003c\u003d this-\u003eoffset().fX + runOffsetInLine + run-\u003eadvance().fX` in RTL fixes it.",
